\description{
An Icechunk repository seen through DBI. Tables are the byterefs
projection of the snapshot the connection is pinned to (see
\code{\link[=ic_to_byterefs]{ic_to_byterefs()}}): \code{meta}, \code{arrays}, \code{sources} and one \verb{refs_<array>}
per data array, plus Icechunk's own \code{branches}, \code{tags}, \code{ancestry} and
\code{nodes}. SQL (\code{\link[DBI:dbGetQuery]{DBI::dbGetQuery()}}) runs on an in-memory SQLite copy of
the tables a statement names (requires RSQLite).
}
\details{
Writes go through a writable session on the connection's branch:
\code{\link[DBI:dbBegin]{DBI::dbBegin()}} opens it, \code{\link[DBI:dbAppendTable]{DBI::dbAppendTable()}} on \verb{refs_<array>} sets
virtual (or inline, from \code{data}) chunk refs, on \code{arrays} creates arrays,
\code{\link[DBI:dbCommit]{DBI::dbCommit()}} commits (pass \code{message}), \code{\link[DBI:dbRollback]{DBI::dbRollback()}}
discards. Without \code{dbBegin()} each append commits on its own.
}
